# Next.js web conventions

## Data fetching

All API calls go through the existing wrappers in `src/lib` (`api()` in `lib/api.ts`, or the domain wrappers `musicFetch`/`watchFetch`/`readFetch`, `authApi`, `enterprise-api`) wrapped in TanStack React Query (`useQuery`/`useMutation`). Never call raw `fetch()` inside a component or page. For live data use the existing SSE hooks (`useSseBackedQuery`, etc.), not polling loops.

## Types come from shared

API response/request shapes are `import type { X } from "@questorylabs/shared"`. Do not re-declare local interfaces for API payloads (`AppShell`'s local `MeResponse` instead of the shared user schema is the anti-pattern — don't copy it). If a shape is missing from shared, add it there.

## Feature gating

Soft-gated routes (`/music/*`, `/watch/*`, `/read/*`, `/recommendations`, `/admin/telemetry`) are gated by the existing components/hooks: `MusicGate`, `WatchGate`, `ReadGate`, `EnterpriseGate` in layouts, and `useMusicEnabled`/`useWatchEnabled`/`useReadEnabled`/`useEnterpriseEnabled` for conditional UI. Never read feature-flag env vars or `/health` flags inline in a page.

## Components and pages

- Reuse `components/ui/*` primitives first (`Button`, `Dialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Panel`, `StateMessage`, `OverflowMarquee`). New generic UI goes in `components/ui` (re-export from `ui/index.ts`); domain UI goes in `components/<domain>/`.
- A `page.tsx` wires queries to components — keep it well under 400 lines. The 650–750 line music/watch settings pages are the anti-pattern; extract sections into components instead.
- Before building a music/watch/read variant of an existing component (pickers, insights charts, detail pages), generalize the existing one and parameterize the domain — do not add another near-identical copy.

## Destructive actions require confirmation

Any action that deletes, overwrites, re-runs, or otherwise mutates existing data (delete user, run/retry a migration, trigger a sync that rewrites imports, discard a draft) must show a confirmation step before the mutation fires. Use the shared `Dialog` from `components/ui` with a Cancel + confirm button pair — the `/admin/migrations` run/retry dialog is the reference pattern. Never wire a destructive `onClick` straight to `mutation.mutate(...)`, and do not use `window.confirm` for new code.

## Shared constants, not inline literals

Tunable constants (page sizes, limits, polling intervals, thresholds) live in a shared `src/lib` module and are imported where needed — `lib/pagination.ts` is the reference pattern for page sizes. Do not declare `const PAGE_SIZE = 25` (or similar) inside a page/component/hook; add it to the appropriate shared file (or create one per concern) and import it. One shared definition means one place to tune the value app-wide.

## Styling

Tailwind v4 utility classes plus the CSS variables defined in `globals.css` (`--ink`, `--accent`, fonts). No new CSS modules (the only existing ones are legacy under `components/enterprise/`), no inline style objects for things Tailwind covers.

## App Router

Routes live under `src/app` with the `(app)`/`(admin)` route groups and their shells. Follow the existing client-component + React Query pattern for pages; do not introduce one-off server-side data fetching patterns without need.
